==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/məʊ/|a=UK}}
* {{enPR|mō|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/moʊ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-mo.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊ|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|mo}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mā}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*maiz}}, from a comparative form of {{der|en|ine-pro|*meh₂-}}. Cognate with {{cog|sv|mer}}, {{cog|da|mer}}; and with {{cog|ga|mó}}, {{cog|sq|më}}. See also {{m|en|more}}, {{m|en|most}}.

====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To a greater degree.
#* {{RQ:Erasmus Udall Apophthegmes|chapter=Aristippus|folio=43|verso=yes|para=42|passage=When he had ſaied no: what (ſaid Ariſtippus) is it ſhame to ſaile in a Shippe, that hath afoꝛetymes caried a great nomber '''mo''': {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|now|_|dialectal}} [[further|Further]], [[longer]].

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|archaic|dialectal}} [[greater|Greater]] in amount, quantity, or number ''(of discrete objects, as opposed to [[more]], which was applied to substances)''
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c. 1380|author=William Langland|title=Piers Plowman
|passage=With that ran there a route of ratones at ones,<br>And smale mys myd hem, '''mo''' then a thousande}}
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|Matthew|22|passage=Nether durste eny man from that daye forth axe hym eny '''moo''' questions.}}

===Etymology 2===
{{clipping|en|month}}.

====Symbol====
{{head|en|symbol}}

# {{senseid|en|Q5151}} [[month#English:_Q5151|month]]
#: {{alti|en|mo.<id:Q5151>|mon<id:Q5151>|mul:m<id:Q5151>|mul:M<id:Q5151>}}
#: {{ux|en|12 yr 4 '''mo''' 17 d}}

===Etymology 3===

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} {{clipping of|en|moment}}.
#: {{syn|en|bit|sec|tick|Thesaurus:moment}}
#: {{ux|en|Hang on a '''mo'''!}}

===Etymology 4===
{{clipping|en|homo}}, itself a short form of {{m|en|homosexual}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[homosexual]].

===Etymology 5===
{{nrhot|en|more}}. Only coincidentally similar to sense 1 [[#Etymology_1|above]]. Compare {{m|en|fo'|t=for; four}}, {{m|en|ho|t=whore|id=whore}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{senseid|en|more}} {{lb|en|dialectal|AAVE}} {{alternative form of|en|mo'|t=more}}.
#: {{ux|en|Yo, you got '''mo''' chips?}}

===Etymology 6===
{{clipping|en|moustache}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Australia|New Zealand|colloquial}} A [[moustache]].

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|en|Movember}}

===Etymology 7===
Clipping.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|prison slang}} A [[molester]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=James Kühnel|title=Carceration State
|passage=The Idaho prison is full of ''cho-mos'' (child molesters), '''''mos''''' (molesters), and all types of sexual predators that have engaged in some type of abnormal sexual acts.}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|chomo}}

===Etymology 8===
Clipping.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[moron]].

===Etymology 9===
From [[mil]], by analogy with [[do]] and [[gro]].

====Numeral====
{{head|en|numeral}}

# The [[cardinal number]] occurring after [[el]] [[gro]] [[el]] [[do]] [[el]] (↋↋↋) and before mo [[one]] (1001) in a [[duodecimal]] system. Written 1000, decimal value 1728.

====See also====
* {{l|en|do}}, {{l|en|gro}}

